1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:02,350
Elias's paper had his obituary.

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:05,070
It arrived a day
early: his name,

3
00:00:05,270 --> 00:00:07,510
his apartment, a fire at 3:07.

4
00:00:08,350 --> 00:00:09,030
He was alive.

5
00:00:10,276 --> 00:00:11,186
He had no subscription.

6
00:00:11,216 --> 00:00:13,326
Underneath, in small print:

7
00:00:13,356 --> 00:00:15,096
one name per fire.

8
00:00:15,615 --> 00:00:18,235
At 2:40, Elias knocked on 4A.

9
00:00:18,855 --> 00:00:20,815
Mara's heater had been
sparking all week.

10
00:00:21,135 --> 00:00:22,455
She'd asked him to fix it.

11
00:00:22,715 --> 00:00:24,055
He told her to call the super.

12
00:00:24,555 --> 00:00:25,325
He took the stairs

13
00:00:25,355 --> 00:00:26,535
and didn't look back.

14
00:00:26,915 --> 00:00:27,885
From the hotel, he

15
00:00:27,915 --> 00:00:29,275
watched the smoke rise.

16
00:00:29,915 --> 00:00:32,015
At 3:07, 4B burned.

17
00:00:32,655 --> 00:00:33,565
The next paper waited

18
00:00:33,595 --> 00:00:34,655
at the front desk.

19
00:00:35,075 --> 00:00:36,035
Same fire.

20
00:00:36,315 --> 00:00:37,095
Same hour.

21
00:00:37,275 --> 00:00:37,995
Different name.

22
00:00:39,165 --> 00:00:40,055
Mara Kwan.

23
00:00:40,085 --> 00:00:41,445
Apartment 4A.

24
00:00:41,665 --> 00:00:42,475
It said she'd entered

25
00:00:42,505 --> 00:00:43,925
4B to warn him.

26
00:00:44,485 --> 00:00:45,255
Elias laid the two

27
00:00:45,285 --> 00:00:47,145
obituaries side by side.

28
00:00:47,485 --> 00:00:48,135
His name.

29
00:00:48,345 --> 00:00:49,085
Mara's.

30
00:00:49,906 --> 00:00:51,966
The paper wasn't
predicting the future.

31
00:00:52,426 --> 00:00:54,366
It was choosing who paid for it.
